The error message is telling you that the feature you are using is only available in C++20. The "using enum" keyword is a feature that was introduced in C++20. 

The reason it does not recognise add, subtract etc. is because the "using enum" keyword is not importing the enum values into the current scope. It is importing the enum values into the current scope as if they were defined with the "enum class" syntax. 

So, if you have an enum like this:

enum class Operation {
 add,
 subtract,
 multiply,
 divide
};

The "using enum" keyword would import the enum values into the current scope like this:

enum class Operation {
 add,
 subtract,
 multiply,
 divide
};

using enum Operation;

// This is equivalent to:
enum class Operation {
 add,
 subtract,
 multiply,
 divide
};



